Gaster switches Apple devices with A5-A11 SoCs into the extended DFU
access mode through the checkm8 boot ROM mechanism. In this mode the
boot ROM accepts unsigned images, which is the entry point for booting
alternative operating systems from a host over USB.

The phone rescue kit uses it to give unsupported Apple phones a second
life with EmberBSD. The whole sequence runs in RAM: gaster never writes
to device storage.

This package builds the native NetBSD backend on the ugen interface,
with the pre-generated boot ROM payload headers from files/. The
leakprobe and portreset host tools from the same kit help with the
extended DFU access diagnostics.
